< - **R-STB (entry into `STANDBY`, ruling R1):** every row from another state into `STANDBY` checks the facts first: battery at B2 goes to `OFF`, at B5 to `ERR_BATTERY_LOW`, free space at SFULL to `ERR_STORAGE_FULL` (battery first). It does so through the row of `STANDBY` for that event ("battery reaches B2", "battery reaches B5", "free space at SFULL"), with that row's actions. This covers the rows `TRANSFER` VBUS removed, `ERR_STORAGE_FAULT` storage retry succeeds, `ERR_MIC_FAULT` 5 s elapsed and `ERR_CHARGER` VBUS removed.
< - **Order at "init done" (rulings R4, R5, correction R4b):** at B2 (no VBUS) the row "battery at B2 and no VBUS" (to `OFF`, no recovery: the open flag stays set and the next start-up recovers); else a start-up with an unfinished recording takes the row "init done, superblock open flag set" first (`RECOVERY`); at the end of the scan the battery rule applies: "scan done, VBUS present" goes to `CHARGING`, "scan done, no VBUS" enters `STANDBY` through rule R-STB (at B5 to `ERR_BATTERY_LOW`); else at B5 (no VBUS) the row "battery at B5 and no VBUS" (to `ERR_BATTERY_LOW`); else the row "init done, superblock open flag clear, no VBUS, battery above B5" or "init done, VBUS present".
